  "textContent": "The second day of rehearsals for the television special James Paul McCartney took place on 7 March 1973. Rehearsals and filming took place at Elstree Studios. On this day Wings were in the studio to rehearse their concert sequence, which was filmed on 18 March. The rehearsals were filmed, and the audio was used for the final soundtrack.Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 28 November 2025Also on this day...1999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Berkeley Community Theatre, Berkeley1990: Paul McCartney live: Tokyo Dome, Tokyo1982: Recording: Alibi by Ringo Starr1975: Recording: Rock Show by Wings1973: Recording: Oh My My by Ringo Starr1972: Recording: When The Night by Wings1967: Recording: Lovely Rita1965: Filming: Help!, the Bahamas1963: The Beatles live: Mersey Beat Showcase, Nottingham1962: Radio: Teenager’s Turn – Here We Go – The Beatles’ first radio session1961: The Beatles live: Cassanova Club, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
